  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "For an **upper-upscale positioning strategy in North America**, an owner should typically consider brands from the major chains that are widely recognized or listed in that tier: **Marriott** (Marriott Hotels, Sheraton, Westin, Le Méridien, Renaissance, Delta Hotels, Autograph Collection, Tribute Portfolio), **Hilton** (Hilton Hotels & Resorts, Signia by Hilton, Curio Collection, DoubleTree, Embassy Suites, Canopy), **Hyatt** (Grand Hyatt, Hyatt Regency, Hyatt, Thompson, Destination by Hyatt, The Unbound Collection, JdV by Hyatt, Dream Hotels), **IHG** (Crowne Plaza, HUALUXE), **Accor** (Pullman, Swissôtel, Mövenpick, MGallery, 21c), **Wyndham** (Wyndham Grand, Dolce by Wyndham), **Sonesta** (Royal Sonesta, The James), **Best Western** (WorldHotels Elite, WorldHotels Distinctive), **Choice** (Radisson Blu), and **Margaritaville Hotels and Resorts**.[7][5]\n\nIf you want a shorter “shortlist” based on North American chain-scale examples, STR’s upper-upscale set includes brands such as **Grand Hyatt, Marriott Hotels, Autograph Collection, Hilton, Wyndham Grand, Dolce, EVENS Hotels, Four Points by Sheraton, Grand America, Eurostars, and JW Marriott** among others.[4][14][5]\n\nA practical way to think about the opportunity is:\n\n- **Classic full-service upper-upscale:** Marriott Hotels, Sheraton, Westin, Hilton, Hyatt Regency, Grand Hyatt, InterContinental-adjacent competitive set, Crowne Plaza.[7][10]\n- **Lifestyle/soft-brand upper-upscale:** Autograph Collection, Tribute Portfolio, Curio Collection, The Unbound Collection, JdV by Hyatt, MGallery, The James, Royal Sonesta.[7]\n- **Upper-upscale extended-stay/suite-oriented:** Embassy Suites, Homewood Suites-adjacent competitive set, and some Marriott/Hyatt upper-upscale conversion plays depending on market.[7][10]\n- **High-performing recognized names in North America:** Margaritaville, Kimpton, Hyatt Centric, Omni are repeatedly surfaced in rating/ranking lists for the segment.[2]\n\nIf you are evaluating an ownership case, the most relevant brands usually depend on whether the asset is best suited for **full-service, lifestyle, conversion, or resort** positioning, since upper-upscale brand families differ a lot on required product, amenity load, and fee structure.[7][9][10]",
